| Expenses:Auto          | Expense | true        |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel     | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Auto:Repairs  | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount   | Date       | Payee         | Destination            | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Checking | 2023-06-30 | Acme Payroll  | Income:Salary          | 40000.00 |
| T2  | Assets:Checking | 2023-07-15 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries     | -400.00  |
| T3  | Assets:Checking | 2023-08-10 | Shell         | Expenses:Auto:Fuel     | -120.00  |
| T4  | Assets:Checking | 2024-02-28 | Acme Payroll  | Income:Salary          | 42000.00 |
| T5  | Assets:Checking | 2024-03-15 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries     | -500.00  |
| T6  | Assets:Checking | 2024-04-10 | Shell         | Expenses:Auto:Fuel     | -150.00  |
| T7  | Assets:Checking | 2024-05-05 | Quick Fit     | Expenses:Auto:Repairs  | -300.00  |
| T8  | Assets:Checking | 2024-06-30 | First Bank    | Income:Interest        | 25.00    |
| T9  | Assets:Checking | 2024-07-01 | Unknown       | Expenses:Uncategorized | -10.00   |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# By category
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario A category report for one year
Description The tree is kept, with a subtotal on every placeholder, and income
# and expenses both read as positive figures.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given transactions are as previous
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2024-01-01 |
| To       | 2024-12-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account                | Level | Amount   | IsSubtotal |
| Income                 | 0     | 42025.00 | true       |
| Income:Interest        | 1     | 25.00    | false      |
| Income:Salary          | 1     | 42000.00 | false      |
| Expenses               | 0     | 960.00   | true       |
| Expenses:Auto          | 1     | 450.00   | true       |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel     | 2     | 150.00   | false      |
| Expenses:Auto:Repairs  | 2     | 300.00   | false      |
| Expenses:Groceries     | 1     | 500.00   | false      |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | 1     | 10.00    | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 42025.00 |
| TotalExpenses | 960.00   |
| Net           | 41065.00 |

Attributes ReportTotal
| Attribute     | Type  | Default |
| TotalIncome   | Money | 0.00    |
| TotalExpenses | Money | 0.00    |
| Net           | Money | 0.00    |

Scenario Quicken signs show expenses negative
Description The same report as above with QuickenSigns asked for, which is how
# Quicken writes it: income positive, expenses negative. For reading
# a figure against a Quicken report side by side, where having to
# negate one column in your head is where mistakes come from.
Details The rule is uniform and has no special cases: a Quicken expense figure
# is the negation of ours, every row, and that holds for a category whose
# figure is a credit as well. Measured on the 2021 business report, where
# Clear Out Balances reads 127.56 in Quicken and -127.56 here, and
# Groceries reads -12,129.60 there and 12,129.60 here.
#
# The net does not move. Only the sign of the expenses figure does, so
# the net is income plus expenses in this mode and income minus expenses
# in the other, and both come to the same number.
#
# Income is untouched because the two conventions already agree on it.
# Payee reports keep the other convention whatever this is set to: a
# payee report sums a payee's income and expense transactions into one
# figure, so a payee with both has no sensible sign here, and flipping it
# would make the number meaningless rather than differently signed.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given transactions are as previous
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy      | Category   |
| From         | 2024-01-01 |
| To           | 2024-12-31 |
| Interval     | Whole      |
| QuickenSigns | true       |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account                | Level | Amount   | IsSubtotal |
| Income                 | 0     | 42025.00 | true       |
| Income:Interest        | 1     | 25.00    | false      |
| Income:Salary          | 1     | 42000.00 | false      |
| Expenses               | 0     | -960.00  | true       |
| Expenses:Auto          | 1     | -450.00  | true       |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel     | 2     | -150.00  | false      |
| Expenses:Auto:Repairs  | 2     | -300.00  | false      |
| Expenses:Groceries     | 1     | -500.00  | false      |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | 1     | -10.00   | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 42025.00 |
| TotalExpenses | -960.00  |
| Net           | 41065.00 |
# Every figure is the one in the scenario above with the expense rows negated,
# and the net is unchanged at 41065.00.

Scenario Rows are in alphabetical order within each parent
Description Not by amount. A report compared with the same report from last
# month should have its rows in the same places, so that the eye can
# find a line without reading every one of them.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path           | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking | Checking | false       |
| Expenses       | Expense | true        |
| Expenses:Zoo   | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Apples | Expense | false      |
| Expenses:Milk  | Expense | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount   | Date       | Payee  | Destination     | Amount  |
