Scenario Asking for the highest categories only shows one line for each
Description The summary: Auto reads 450.00 with nothing under it, and the figure
# still adds to the same total as the full tree. The section lines stay,
# because the totals have to be somewhere.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given transactions are as previous
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category    |
| From     | 2024-01-01  |
| To       | 2024-12-31  |
| Interval | Whole       |
| Detail   | HighestOnly |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account                | Level | Amount   | IsSubtotal |
| Income                 | 0     | 42025.00 | true       |
| Income:Interest        | 1     | 25.00    | false      |
| Income:Salary          | 1     | 42000.00 | false      |
| Expenses               | 0     | 960.00   | true       |
| Expenses:Auto          | 1     | 450.00   | false      |
| Expenses:Groceries     | 1     | 500.00   | false      |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | 1     | 10.00    | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 42025.00 |
| TotalExpenses | 960.00   |
| Net           | 41065.00 |
# The same rows as the depth-limit scenario above, which is the point:
# HighestOnly is Depth 1 under the name the report offers. Auto is a leaf here,
# so it is not marked a subtotal even though its 450.00 came from below.

Scenario Asking for all the categories shows the whole tree indented
Description Every category, each one starting a step further over than its
# parent, so that Fuel reads as part of Auto without the path having to
# be written out on the line. The indent is Level: one step per level,
# and a transaction line later takes its indent the same way.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given transactions are as previous
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category      |
| From     | 2024-01-01    |
| To       | 2024-12-31    |
| Interval | Whole         |
| Detail   | AllCategories |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account                | Level | Amount   | IsSubtotal |
| Income                 | 0     | 42025.00 | true       |
| Income:Interest        | 1     | 25.00    | false      |
| Income:Salary          | 1     | 42000.00 | false      |
| Expenses               | 0     | 960.00   | true       |
| Expenses:Auto          | 1     | 450.00   | true       |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel     | 2     | 150.00   | false      |
| Expenses:Auto:Repairs  | 2     | 300.00   | false      |
| Expenses:Groceries     | 1     | 500.00   | false      |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | 1     | 10.00    | false      |
# AllCategories is what a report with nothing asked for shows, which is why the
# first scenario in this file reads the same without naming it.

Attributes ReportDetailLine
Description One line of a report shown with its transactions.
Details Two amount columns, because they are two different kinds of figure and
# putting them in one column would invite adding a transaction to the
# total that already contains it. Each holds the individual amount and is
# filled only on a transaction line; Amount holds the figure for the
# category and is filled only on a category line. Each is the left of the
# two, so the individual amounts run down the inside of the page and the
# column of totals stays where it is in every other report.
#
# A column with nothing in it on this line is empty rather than zero: a
# category line has no individual amount to show, which is not the same as
# showing it as 0.00.
#
# Account on a transaction line is the category the transaction was posted
# to, so that a line can be read on its own, and Level is one more than
# that category's, which is what steps it over.
| Attribute | Type           | Default |
| Kind      | ReportLineKind |         |
| Account   | AccountPath    |         |
| Level     | Integer        | 0       |
| Date      | Date           |         |
| Payee     | PayeeName      |         |
| Each      | Money          |         |
| Amount    | Money          |         |

DataType ReportLineKind
Description What a line of a report shown with its transactions is.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value       | Notes                                                     |
| Category    | A category or a section, carrying the figure beneath it    |
| Other       | The Other line standing for a category's own transactions  |
| Transaction | One transaction, under the line whose figure it is part of |

Scenario Asking for transactions shows each one under its category
Description The figures are the ones the full tree already shows; what is added is
# a line for each transaction behind them, in date order, one step
# further over than the category it belongs to.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given transactions are as previous
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category     |
| From     | 2024-01-01   |
| To       | 2024-12-31   |
| Interval | Whole        |
| Detail   | Transactions |
Then report lines are : ReportDetailLine
| Kind        | Account                | Level | Date       | Payee         | Each     | Amount   |
| Category    | Income                 | 0     |            |               |          | 42025.00 |
| Category    | Income:Interest        | 1     |            |               |          | 25.00    |
| Transaction | Income:Interest        | 2     | 2024-06-30 | First Bank    | 25.00    |          |
| Category    | Income:Salary          | 1     |            |               |          | 42000.00 |
| Transaction | Income:Salary          | 2     | 2024-02-28 | Acme Payroll  | 42000.00 |          |
| Category    | Expenses               | 0     |            |               |          | 960.00   |
| Category    | Expenses:Auto          | 1     |            |               |          | 450.00   |
| Category    | Expenses:Auto:Fuel     | 2     |            |               |          | 150.00   |
| Transaction | Expenses:Auto:Fuel     | 3     | 2024-04-10 | Shell         | 150.00   |          |
| Category    | Expenses:Auto:Repairs  | 2     |            |               |          | 300.00   |
| Transaction | Expenses:Auto:Repairs  | 3     | 2024-05-05 | Quick Fit     | 300.00   |          |
| Category    | Expenses:Groceries     | 1     |            |               |          | 500.00   |
| Transaction | Expenses:Groceries     | 2     | 2024-03-15 | Harris Teeter | 500.00   |          |
| Category    | Expenses:Uncategorized | 1     |            |               |          | 10.00    |
| Transaction | Expenses:Uncategorized | 2     | 2024-07-01 | Unknown       | 10.00    |          |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 42025.00 |
| TotalExpenses | 960.00   |
| Net           | 41065.00 |
# A transaction line takes the display sign of its category, as every other
# figure in a report does, so the salary reads 42000.00 and not -42000.00.
# Transactions under one category are in date order, and two on the same date
# keep the order the register has them in.
#
# Nothing is shown under a section line or a placeholder: Expenses has no
# transactions of its own, and the lines beneath it still add to its 960.00.

Scenario A category with transactions of its own shows them under its Other line
Description The Other line is where a category's own transactions are totalled,
# so it is where they are listed. Without that, the forty and the ten
# would both hang under Auto and the page would not say which of them
# the Other line stood for.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Checking | false       |
| Expenses:Auto      | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel | Expense | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount   | Date       | Payee    | Destination        | Amount |
| T1  | Assets:Checking | 2026-03-01 | Shell    | Expenses:Auto:Fuel | -40.00 |
| T2  | Assets:Checking | 2026-03-02 | Car Wash | Expenses:Auto      | -10.00 |
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category     |
| From     | 2026-01-01   |
| To       | 2026-12-31   |
| Detail   | Transactions |
Then report lines are : ReportDetailLine
| Kind        | Account            | Level | Date       | Payee    | Each  | Amount |
| Category    | Expenses           | 0     |            |          |       | 50.00  |
| Category    | Expenses:Auto      | 1     |            |          |       | 50.00  |
| Category    | Expenses:Auto:Fuel | 2     |            |          |       | 40.00  |
| Transaction | Expenses:Auto:Fuel | 3     | 2026-03-01 | Shell    | 40.00 |        |
| Other       | Other Auto         | 2     |            |          |       | 10.00  |
| Transaction | Expenses:Auto      | 3     | 2026-03-02 | Car Wash | 10.00 |        |
# The transaction line names the category it was posted to -- Expenses:Auto --
# because that is what was chosen for it. Other Auto is the report's own line
# and nothing is posted to it, which is why it has a kind of its own here.
#
# The Expenses line is there although this chart never declares Expenses: it is
# an ancestor of a category that is declared, and a report heads a subtree with
# a line whether or not anybody wrote the placeholder down.

Scenario Transfers do not appear in a category report
Description A transfer between two real accounts touches no category, so it is
# absent without having to be excluded. This is the reason the credit
# card payment in Transactions is modelled as a transfer: were it an
# expense, this report would count the same spending twice.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Checking   | false       |
| Assets:Savings     | Checking   | false       |
| Liabilities:Visa   | CreditCard | false       |
| Expenses           | Expense    | true        |
| Expenses:Shopping  | Expense    | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount    | Date       | Payee    | Destination       | Amount  |
| T1  | Liabilities:Visa | 2024-03-02 | Amazon   | Expenses:Shopping | -89.99  |
| T2  | Liabilities:Visa | 2024-03-25 | Visa     | Assets:Checking   | 300.00  |
| T3  | Assets:Checking  | 2024-03-28 | Transfer | Assets:Savings    | -500.00 |
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2024-01-01 |
| To       | 2024-12-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account           | Level | Amount | IsSubtotal |
| Expenses          | 0     | 89.99  | true       |
| Expenses:Shopping | 1     | 89.99  | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 0.00  |
| TotalExpenses | 89.99 |
| Net           | -89.99 |

