| Expenses                | 55.00  | 0     | true       |
| Expenses:Auto           | 55.00  | 1     | true       |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel      | 40.00  | 2     | false      |
| Expenses:Auto:Insurance | 15.00  | 2     | false      |
# Nothing was posted to Auto, so there is no Other row and the two children add
# to the total above them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Investment activity
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

BusinessRule Income and expense arising inside an investment account is left out
Description A spending report answers what was earned and spent. A dividend
# reinvested inside a retirement account was neither: no money
# reached the household, and the figure is reported on a 1099
# rather than budgeted against.
Details
# So the test is not which category was used but where the money was.
# A category transaction counts when the transaction it belongs to touches
# no investment account, and is left out when it touches one. The same
# category can do both -- Invest Inc is real income when the dividend
# lands in a bank account and is not when it stays in the brokerage --
# which is why the category alone cannot decide it.
#
# Money actually moved out of an investment account into a bank account
# is a transfer between two real accounts, so it never reached this
# report in the first place; see the transfer scenario above.
#
# IncludeInvestmentActivity puts it all back, for the reader who wants
# the whole picture rather than the household one.
Examples: InvestmentActivityCase
| TransactionTouches                     | Category          | Counts | Notes                               |
| A brokerage account only               | Income:Invest Inc | false  | A dividend reinvested; on the 1099  |
| A retirement account only              | Income:Invest Inc | false  | Same, and not yet taxable           |
| A brokerage account and a bank account | Income:Invest Inc | false  | The brokerage side taints it        |
| A bank account only                    | Income:Invest Inc | true   | A dividend paid out and spendable   |
| A brokerage account only               | Expenses:Fees     | false  | An advisory fee taken from the fund |
| A bank account only                    | Expenses:Fees     | true   | A fee paid by cheque                |

Attributes InvestmentActivityCase
| Attribute          | Type        | Default |
| TransactionTouches | String      |         |
| Category           | AccountPath |         |
| Counts             | Boolean     | false   |
| Notes              | String      | none    |

Scenario A dividend reinvested inside a retirement account is not income
Description T2 credits Income:Invest Inc for 1200.00 and the money stayed in
# the IRA, so the report shows only the 40.00 that reached the bank.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path              | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking   | Checking   | false       |
| Assets:Ken IRA    | Brokerage  | false       |
| Income            | Income     | true        |
| Income:Invest Inc | Income     | false       |
| Income:Salary     | Income     | false       |
| Expenses          | Expense    | true        |
| Expenses:Fees     | Expense    | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount   | Date       | Payee        | Destination       | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Checking | 2024-03-01 | Acme Payroll | Income:Salary     | 5000.00  |
| T2  | Assets:Ken IRA  | 2024-03-02 | Vanguard     | Income:Invest Inc | 1200.00  |
| T3  | Assets:Checking | 2024-03-03 | First Bank   | Income:Invest Inc | 40.00    |
| T4  | Assets:Ken IRA  | 2024-03-04 | Vanguard     | Expenses:Fees     | -25.00   |
| T5  | Assets:Ken IRA  | 2024-03-05 | Vanguard     | Assets:Checking   | -3000.00 |
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2024-01-01 |
| To       | 2024-12-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account           | Level | Amount  | IsSubtotal |
| Income            | 0     | 5040.00 | true       |
| Income:Invest Inc | 1     | 40.00   | false      |
| Income:Salary     | 1     | 5000.00 | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 5040.00 |
| TotalExpenses | 0.00    |
| Net           | 5040.00 |
# The 25.00 advisory fee came out of the IRA too, so there are no expense rows
# at all. T5 is a transfer between two real accounts and was never a candidate.

