# zero against it.

Scenario A draw from another book does not reach the spending report
Description Money drawn from Ken Pugh, Inc. or WarpandByteDesigns is not income
# here. That income was earned and already reported in the other
# book, and counting it again would state the same earnings twice.
# Entered as a transfer to an account for what that entity has paid
# across, both sides are real, so nothing has to exclude it: only the
# salary was earned in this book.
Details
# The convention, rather than a mechanism. A draw is entered as this
# transfer when it happens; nothing rewrites a category on import, and
# the import stays a faithful mirror of its source. Twenty years of
# history hold two such transactions -- 27,500.00 drawn in December 2021
# and 10,815.00 returned in August 2022 -- so a mapping in the importer
# would be machinery for two lines, and a rule that applied only after
# some cutover date would put a step in the middle of the multi-year
# report that is the point of keeping the history at all.
#
# The reimbursement trees that carry the same two names are a different
# thing and need nothing: a business expense paid personally debits a
# subcategory and the reimbursement credits the parent, so the subtree
# cancels itself. Over 2010 to 2026 the Warp And Byte tree nets 230.94
# across 3,540 transactions. What is left in such a net is a real personal
# expense that was never reimbursed, so excluding it would be wrong.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                         | Type   | Placeholder |
| Assets:Ken~Checking          | Checking | false       |
| Assets:Due~from~Ken~Pugh~Inc | OtherAsset | false       |
| Income                       | Income | true        |
| Income:Salary~Ken            | Income | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount       | Date       | Payee                      | Destination                  | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Ken~Checking | 2021-03-15 | Transfer from Ken Pugh Inc | Assets:Due~from~Ken~Pugh~Inc | 27500.00 |
| T2  | Assets:Ken~Checking | 2021-03-31 | Acme Payroll               | Income:Salary~Ken            | 1800.00  |
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2021-01-01 |
| To       | 2021-12-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account           | Level | Amount  | IsSubtotal |
| Income            | 0     | 1800.00 | true       |
| Income:Salary~Ken | 1     | 1800.00 | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 1800.00 |
| TotalExpenses | 0.00    |
| Net           | 1800.00 |
# The 27,500.00 is absent, and the balance of Assets:Due from Ken Pugh Inc is
# where it can be read instead.

