# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A balance sheet
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description What is owned and what is owed, as at one date, with net worth as
# the bottom line.
Details Every other report in this file totals a period. A balance sheet is a
# position: a balance is as at a moment, so From is not read and To is
# the date the sheet is drawn up as at. Interval Whole and GroupBy
# Account say that this is the one-column form; the same report with
# Interval Year is the net worth table further down, which is this
# bottom line as at several dates at once.
#
# The two sides are the real accounts, divided by the side each type is
# on: see the balance-side rule in CoreTypes, which is the only place the
# words Asset and Liability decide anything. The groups and their order
# are the ones the account list uses, so the page and the list down the
# side of the window agree with each other, and a group with nothing in
# it is left out rather than shown empty.
#
# The Transfer group is left out altogether. Those accounts hold money on
# its way between two accounts that are both already here, so showing
# them would count the same money twice.
#
# Each figure is the display balance, so a card and a mortgage read as
# what is owed rather than as the negative balances they are posted as,
# and net worth is what is owned less what is owed.
#
# The categories are not here. Income, Expenses and Equity are nominal,
# and a balance sheet is the real accounts -- but the equity that started
# the book and everything earned and spent since are exactly what net
# worth is made of, which is the last scenario in this section.

Attributes BalanceSheetRow
Description One line of a balance sheet. A group heading carries the total of
# the accounts under it and names no account; an account names no
# group. Level is the indent, as in the account list: a heading is 0,
# an account under it 1, and a child of that account 2.
| Attribute  | Type                | Default |
| Section    | BalanceSheetSection | Assets  |
| Group      | Text                | none    |
| Account    | AccountPath         | none    |
| Level      | Integer             | 0       |
| Balance    | Money               | 0.00    |
| IsHeading  | Boolean             | false   |
| IsSubtotal | Boolean             | false   |

DataType BalanceSheetSection
Description The two sides of a balance sheet.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value       | Notes                                                   |
| Assets      | What is owned: Banking, Investments and Assets          |
| Liabilities | What is owed: CreditCards and Liabilities               |

Scenario A balance sheet as at a date
Description A house and a mortgage, a card and two bank accounts. The salary
# that arrives in March is not on a sheet drawn up in February: a
# balance as at a date ignores what happens after it.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                    | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking         | Checking   | false       |
| Assets:Savings          | Savings    | false       |
| Assets:House            | RealEstate | false       |
| Liabilities:Visa        | CreditCard | false       |
| Liabilities:Mortgage    | Mortgage   | false       |
| Income:Salary           | Income     | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries      | Expense    | false       |
| Equity:Opening Balances | Equity     | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount    | Date       | Payee         | Destination             | Amount    |
| T1  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-01-01 | Opening       | Equity:Opening Balances | 5000.00   |
| T2  | Assets:House     | 2026-01-01 | Opening       | Split                   | 200000.00 |
| T3  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-01-05 | Acme Payroll  | Income:Salary           | 3000.00   |
| T4  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries      | -45.00    |
| T5  | Liabilities:Visa | 2026-01-20 | Amazon        | Expenses:Groceries      | -89.99    |
| T6  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-01-25 | Transfer      | Assets:Savings          | -500.00   |
| T7  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-03-10 | Acme Payroll  | Income:Salary           | 1000.00   |
Given split lines are : TransactionSplit
| Destination             | Amount     |
| Liabilities:Mortgage    | -150000.00 |
| Equity:Opening Balances | -50000.00  |
When balance sheet run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Account    |
| Interval | Whole      |
| To       | 2026-02-28 |
Then balance sheet rows are : BalanceSheetRow
| Section     | Group       | Account              | Level | Balance   | IsHeading | IsSubtotal |
| Assets      | Banking     | none                 | 0     | 7955.00   | true      | false      |
| Assets      | none        | Assets:Checking      | 1     | 7455.00   | false     | false      |
| Assets      | none        | Assets:Savings       | 1     | 500.00    | false     | false      |
| Assets      | Assets      | none                 | 0     | 200000.00 | true      | false      |
| Assets      | none        | Assets:House         | 1     | 200000.00 | false     | false      |
| Liabilities | CreditCards | none                 | 0     | 89.99     | true      | false      |
| Liabilities | none        | Liabilities:Visa     | 1     | 89.99     | false     | false      |
| Liabilities | Liabilities | none                 | 0     | 150000.00 | true      | false      |
| Liabilities | none        | Liabilities:Mortgage | 1     | 150000.00 | false     | false      |
Then balance sheet total is : NetWorth Vertical
| Assets      | 207955.00 |
| Liabilities | 150089.99 |
| NetWorth    | 57865.01  |
# Checking is 5000 in, 3000 of salary, 45 of groceries and 500 moved to
# savings: 7455.00. The March salary is not in it. There is no Investments
# heading because there is nothing in that group, and the categories and
# Equity:Opening Balances are absent -- a balance sheet is the real accounts.

Scenario An account at zero is left out
Description A wallet that has never been used and a card that has been paid off
# are both at zero, and neither earns a line. Twenty years of history
# leaves a trail of closed accounts, and a page of zeroes is a page
# nobody reads.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                    | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking         | Checking   | false       |
| Assets:Wallet           | Cash       | false       |
| Liabilities:Visa        | CreditCard | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries      | Expense    | false       |
| Equity:Opening Balances | Equity     | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount    | Date       | Payee   | Destination             | Amount  |
| T1  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-01-05 | Opening | Equity:Opening Balances | 1000.00 |
| T2  | Liabilities:Visa | 2026-01-10 | Amazon  | Expenses:Groceries      | -50.00  |
| T3  | Liabilities:Visa | 2026-01-20 | Payment | Assets:Checking         | 50.00   |
When balance sheet run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Account    |
| Interval | Whole      |
| To       | 2026-01-31 |
Then balance sheet rows are : BalanceSheetRow
| Section | Group   | Account         | Level | Balance | IsHeading | IsSubtotal |
| Assets  | Banking | none            | 0     | 950.00  | true      | false      |
| Assets  | none    | Assets:Checking | 1     | 950.00  | false     | false      |
Then balance sheet total is : NetWorth Vertical
| Assets      | 950.00 |
| Liabilities | 0.00   |
| NetWorth    | 950.00 |
# The wallet has no transactions at all and the card is back to nothing, so the
# CreditCards heading goes with its only account. The account list down the
# side of the window still shows all three, because that is how an account is
# reached; this is a report, and a report is read rather than navigated.

Scenario Asking for zero rows puts the empty accounts back
Description The same book and date, with ZeroRows asked for, which is the same
# flag the category report uses. A card at zero is worth seeing when
# the question is whether it was paid off.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                    | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking         | Checking   | false       |
| Assets:Wallet           | Cash       | false       |
| Liabilities:Visa        | CreditCard | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries      | Expense    | false       |
| Equity:Opening Balances | Equity     | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount    | Date       | Payee   | Destination             | Amount  |
| T1  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-01-05 | Opening | Equity:Opening Balances | 1000.00 |
| T2  | Liabilities:Visa | 2026-01-10 | Amazon  | Expenses:Groceries      | -50.00  |
| T3  | Liabilities:Visa | 2026-01-20 | Payment | Assets:Checking         | 50.00   |
When balance sheet run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Account    |
| Interval | Whole      |
| To       | 2026-01-31 |
| ZeroRows | true       |
Then balance sheet rows are : BalanceSheetRow
| Section     | Group       | Account          | Level | Balance | IsHeading | IsSubtotal |
| Assets      | Banking     | none             | 0     | 950.00  | true      | false      |
| Assets      | none        | Assets:Checking  | 1     | 950.00  | false     | false      |
| Assets      | none        | Assets:Wallet    | 1     | 0.00    | false     | false      |
| Liabilities | CreditCards | none             | 0     | 0.00    | true      | false      |
| Liabilities | none        | Liabilities:Visa | 1     | 0.00    | false     | false      |
Then balance sheet total is : NetWorth Vertical
| Assets      | 950.00 |
| Liabilities | 0.00   |
| NetWorth    | 950.00 |

Scenario A placeholder carries its subtree, so a brokerage shows its holdings
Description The ordinary roll-up from Accounts, and it is the whole of what a
# balance sheet needs for an investment account: the value of a
# holding is the money balance of its account, so the market value
# arrives through the same addition as everything else. See the
# holding-value rule in Investments.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                    | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Brokerage        | Brokerage  | true        |
| Assets:Brokerage:Cash   | Brokerage  | false       |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX  | Brokerage  | false       |
| Equity:Opening Balances | Equity     | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount          | Date       | Payee   | Destination             | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 2026-01-05 | Opening | Equity:Opening Balances | 13500.00 |
| T2  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2026-01-06 | Buy     | Assets:Brokerage:Cash   | 11000.00 |
When balance sheet run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Account    |
| Interval | Whole      |
| To       | 2026-01-31 |
Then balance sheet rows are : BalanceSheetRow
| Section | Group       | Account                | Level | Balance  | IsHeading | IsSubtotal |
| Assets  | Investments | none                   | 0     | 13500.00 | true      | false      |
| Assets  | none        | Assets:Brokerage       | 1     | 13500.00 | false     | true       |
| Assets  | none        | Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 2     | 2500.00  | false     | false      |
| Assets  | none        | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 2     | 11000.00 | false     | false      |
Then balance sheet total is : NetWorth Vertical
| Assets      | 13500.00 |
| Liabilities | 0.00     |
| NetWorth    | 13500.00 |
# The group heading and the placeholder carry the same 13500.00 here because
# the group holds one top-level account; the heading totals the accounts under
# it and counts each transaction once.
#
# A price that has not been updated makes this figure stale without anything on
# the page saying so, which is what the staleness rule in Investments is for.

Scenario A transfer account is not on the balance sheet
Description A transfer account holds money on its way between two accounts
# that are both already on the sheet, so counting it would count the
# same money twice. It is a real account and it is reconciled like
# one; it is this report that leaves it out. See the balance-side
# rule in CoreTypes.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                    | Type        | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking         | Checking    | false       |
| Assets:In Transit       | TransferIn  | false       |
| Liabilities:Owed Out    | TransferOut | false       |
| Equity:Opening Balances | Equity      | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount        | Date       | Payee   | Destination             | Amount  |
| T1  | Assets:Checking      | 2026-01-05 | Opening | Equity:Opening Balances | 1000.00 |
| T2  | Assets:In Transit    | 2026-01-06 | Moving  | Assets:Checking         | 250.00  |
| T3  | Liabilities:Owed Out | 2026-01-07 | Moving  | Assets:Checking         | -75.00  |
When balance sheet run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Account    |
| Interval | Whole      |
| To       | 2026-01-31 |
Then balance sheet rows are : BalanceSheetRow
| Section | Group   | Account         | Level | Balance | IsHeading | IsSubtotal |
| Assets  | Banking | none            | 0     | 825.00  | true      | false      |
| Assets  | none    | Assets:Checking | 1     | 825.00  | false     | false      |
Then balance sheet total is : NetWorth Vertical
| Assets      | 825.00 |
| Liabilities | 0.00   |
| NetWorth    | 825.00 |
# Checking is 1000.00 less 250.00 on its way out plus 75.00 on its way in. The
# two transfer accounts hold 250.00 and 75.00 between them and neither is on
# the page, so net worth is the checking balance alone -- which is right: the
# money in transit is money the book has already counted once.

Scenario A hidden account with a balance is still on the balance sheet
Description A hidden account is kept out of the pickers so it stops being
# offered, and its money has not gone anywhere. Leaving it out would
# make the sheet disagree with net worth, which is the one thing a
# balance sheet must not do.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                    | Type   | Placeholder | Hidden |
| Assets:Checking         | Checking | false       | false  |
| Assets:Old Savings      | Checking | false       | true   |
| Equity:Opening Balances | Equity | false       | false  |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount      | Date       | Payee   | Destination             | Amount  |
| T1  | Assets:Checking    | 2026-01-05 | Opening | Equity:Opening Balances | 1000.00 |
| T2  | Assets:Old Savings | 2026-01-06 | Opening | Equity:Opening Balances | 250.00  |
When balance sheet run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Account    |
| Interval | Whole      |
| To       | 2026-01-31 |
Then balance sheet rows are : BalanceSheetRow
| Section | Group   | Account            | Level | Balance | IsHeading | IsSubtotal |
| Assets  | Banking | none               | 0     | 1250.00 | true      | false      |
| Assets  | none    | Assets:Checking    | 1     | 1000.00 | false     | false      |
| Assets  | none    | Assets:Old Savings | 1     | 250.00  | false     | false      |
Then balance sheet total is : NetWorth Vertical
| Assets      | 1250.00 |
| Liabilities | 0.00    |
| NetWorth    | 1250.00 |
# The account list leaves this account out until it is asked for; a report
# cannot, because its figures have to add up. See the hidden-account scenarios
# in UserInterface and the hidden-category one earlier in this file, which is
# the same rule for the other side of the book.

Attributes NetWorthTie
Description Net worth taken the other way round, from the nominal accounts.
| Attribute     | Type  | Default |
| OpeningEquity | Money | 0.00    |
| Earned        | Money | 0.00    |
| Spent         | Money | 0.00    |
| NetWorth      | Money | 0.00    |

Scenario Net worth is the opening equity plus what has been earned less spent
Description The same book and date as the first scenario in this section, read
# from the other side. Every transaction balances, so what is owned
# less what is owed must equal what was put into the book plus what
# it has earned and less what it has spent. The two figures agreeing
# is what says the sheet is right, and it is worth showing on the
# page: a difference means a transaction has gone somewhere nobody
# intended, and that is otherwise very hard to see.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                    | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking         | Checking   | false       |
| Assets:Savings          | Savings    | false       |
| Assets:House            | RealEstate | false       |
| Liabilities:Visa        | CreditCard | false       |
| Liabilities:Mortgage    | Mortgage   | false       |
| Income:Salary           | Income     | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries      | Expense    | false       |
| Equity:Opening Balances | Equity     | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount    | Date       | Payee         | Destination             | Amount    |
| T1  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-01-01 | Opening       | Equity:Opening Balances | 5000.00   |
| T2  | Assets:House     | 2026-01-01 | Opening       | Split                   | 200000.00 |
| T3  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-01-05 | Acme Payroll  | Income:Salary           | 3000.00   |
| T4  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries      | -45.00    |
| T5  | Liabilities:Visa | 2026-01-20 | Amazon        | Expenses:Groceries      | -89.99    |
| T6  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-01-25 | Transfer      | Assets:Savings          | -500.00   |
| T7  | Assets:Checking  | 2026-03-10 | Acme Payroll  | Income:Salary           | 1000.00   |
Given split lines are : TransactionSplit
| Destination             | Amount     |
| Liabilities:Mortgage    | -150000.00 |
| Equity:Opening Balances | -50000.00  |
When balance sheet run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Account    |
| Interval | Whole      |
| To       | 2026-02-28 |
Then net worth comes from : NetWorthTie Vertical
| OpeningEquity | 55000.00 |
| Earned        | 3000.00  |
| Spent         | 134.99   |
| NetWorth      | 57865.01 |
# 55,000.00 was put in -- 5,000.00 of cash and the 50,000.00 of equity in the
# house -- 3,000.00 of salary has been earned and 134.99 spent, and 57,865.01
# is the net worth the first scenario reports. The transfer to savings and the
# mortgage are in neither column: moving money between two real accounts
# changes nothing about how much there is.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Net worth over time
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario Net worth at the end of each year
Description The real accounts only, as in Accounts. Each column is a balance as
# at a date rather than a total of a period, which is why this report
# is a different shape from the category one.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path             | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking  | Checking   | false       |
| Liabilities:Visa | CreditCard | false       |
| Income:Salary    | Income     | false       |
| Expenses:Shopping | Expense   | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount    | Date       | Payee        | Destination       | Amount   |
| T1  | Assets:Checking  | 2023-06-30 | Acme Payroll | Income:Salary     | 40000.00 |
| T2  | Liabilities:Visa | 2023-12-01 | Amazon       | Expenses:Shopping | -500.00  |
| T3  | Assets:Checking  | 2024-06-30 | Acme Payroll | Income:Salary     | 42000.00 |
When net worth report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Account    |
| From     | 2023-01-01 |
| To       | 2024-12-31 |
| Interval | Year       |
Then net worth columns are : NetWorthColumn
| AsAt       | Assets   | Liabilities | NetWorth |
| 2023-12-31 | 40000.00 | 500.00      | 39500.00 |
| 2024-12-31 | 82000.00 | 500.00      | 81500.00 |

Attributes NetWorthColumn
| Attribute   | Type  | Default    |
| AsAt        | Date  | 2024-12-31 |
| Assets      | Money | 0.00       |
| Liabilities | Money | 0.00       |
| NetWorth    | Money | 0.00       |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Taking a report away
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario A report is written out as CSV with its figures unrounded
Description The file is for a spreadsheet, so the grouping separators and the
# parentheses of the displayed report are left out and the sign is
# written as a minus.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given transactions are as previous
When report exported as csv : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2024-01-01 |
| To       | 2024-12-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then csv written is
"""
Account,Level,Amount
Income,0,42025.00
Income:Interest,1,25.00
Income:Salary,1,42000.00
Expenses,0,960.00
Expenses:Auto,1,450.00
Expenses:Auto:Fuel,2,150.00
Expenses:Auto:Repairs,2,300.00
Expenses:Groceries,1,500.00
Expenses:Uncategorized,1,10.00
"""
